  "description": "Static world objects of map2_s00 (Old Silent Hill - streets): 60 objects, drawn in file order. An object is drawn while the player is in one of its \"zones\" (each {\"x\": [...], \"z\": [...]} lists 40 m cells along that axis: cell c holds 40c..40(c+1) m; no zones = everywhere) and every flag of \"flags_set\" is set and every flag of \"flags_clear\" is clear (event flag names, e.g. the pickup flags). \"name\" is the object's id for scripts and mods, \"model\" its model (at most 8 characters, the map's or an item model), \"position\" in metres and \"rotation\" in degrees (x, y, z). \"pose\" instead takes position and rotation from a table of the map's overlay on the disc (\"disc_table\" from tables.json, row \"index\"), resolved when the map loads; pickups use it. \"script\": true lets world_objects.lua and events.lua move, turn, re-model or hide the object. \"pc_near_pickup\": true (not in the original) also draws the pickup while the player is in a neighbouring cell of the same floor. Zones are the map's projected cells. BridgeAxle*/Bridge* (the drawbridge) turn with the map variable bridge_rot, SwingingDoor and ChainBroken1/2 with swing_door_rot (world_objects.lua); the locks and keys of Lion, Woodman and Scarecrow show by their flags. A mod's maps/map2_s00/world_objects.json changes or adds objects by name.",
